Local changes since (this model is built from its .sail sources: riscv_sail/Makefile regenerates the C):
- 2026-10-03 model/riscv_fetch_rvfi.sail: the RVFI-DII fetch applies the PMP execute check per 16-bit granule (rvfi_fetch_pmp), as riscv_fetch.sail's mem_read(Execute(), ...) does; the DII fetch reads no memory, so a fetch the PMP denies executed in the model while the core takes an instruction access fault. Found by TestRIG (riscv flavour, opentitan configuration with 16 PMP regions): an mret to U-mode at an address no region matches. Not yet reported upstream.
  The C the bridge compiles (generated_definitions/c/riscv_rvfi_model_RV32.c) is not regenerated by the build, and the Sail 0.19 available locally does not produce C for this sail-0.19.1 runtime (the regenerated C has type errors), so the same check is hand-edited into that C as well: rvfi_fetch_pmp_denied() and its two calls in zfetch(). Tested with a C harness on the bridge: mret to U-mode at 0 then a fetch there traps with mcause 1 (the unpatched C executes it); M-mode fetches with all PMP regions off do not trap.
- 2026-10-10 model/riscv_sys_regs.sail legalize_mstatus: mstatus.FS is cleared (read-only zero) whenever F/D are absent, not only with Zfinx. riscv_sail_cosim_dpi.cc had turned Zfinx on just to get FS read-only zero, which also made the Zfinx encodings (fmadd/fmsub/fnmsub/... on integer registers, opcodes 0x43-0x53) legal in the model; ibex has no float support and traps, so TestRIG riscv-unstructured reported "trap: rtl=1 model=0" (insn 0xfcb3b0cb, 0x6982abc7). Zfinx is now off in the bridge. Hand-edited into the generated C the same way (legalize_mstatus' sys_enable_zfinx() test, `|| !sys_enable_fdext(UNIT)`).
- 2026-10-12 model/riscv_sys_regs.sail haveZicond(): false (was true, with no platform switch). ibex has no Zicond, so czero.eqz/czero.nez executed in the model and trapped on the core (TestRIG riscv_unstructured: "trap: rtl=1 model=0" on 0x0fa1ddb3, 0x0f4bf933). In the generated C the function is inlined into the decoder as `if (true)`: the four guards of the ZICOND_RTYPE matches (EQZ and NEZ, in encdec_backwards and encdec_backwards_infallible) are hand-edited to `if (false)`, each marked "local: haveZicond() = false". Also not in the model sources: init_sys hard-codes misa.S = 1 and misa.A = 1, so riscv_sail_cosim_dpi.cc clears both after zinit_model (ibex has no S-mode and no atomics; stval/sstatus/medeleg and AMO/LR/SC were legal in the model).
- 2026-10-12 model/riscv_sys_regs.sail haveZkr/Zksh/Zksed/Zknh/Zkne/Zknd(): false (were true). ibex implements no scalar crypto, so the AES/SHA/SM3/SM4 encodings executed in the model and trapped on the core (TestRIG riscv_unstructured: "trap: rtl=1 model=0" on aes32esmi 0xe76c8933, aes32dsmi 0x6f5482b3, sha512sig0h 0x5c9d8933, aes32esi 0x23b80733, sm4ks 0x74f20c33). In the generated C these guards are constant-folded away: each of the 18 RV32 decode blocks (SHA256SUM0/1, SHA256SIG0/1, AES32ESI/ESMI/DSI/DSMI, SHA512SUM0R/SUM1R/SIG0L/SIG0H/SIG1L/SIG1H, SM3P0/P1, SM4ED/KS), in encdec_backwards and encdec_backwards_infallible, now starts with a jump to its own no-match label ("local: scalar crypto (Zkn/Zks) off"); is_CSR_defined's seed (0x015) case returns false ("local: haveZkr() = false").
- 2026-10-12 generated C only (no .sail change needed): the RV64-only scalar-crypto encodings (AES64KS1I/KS2/IM/ESM/ES/DSM/DS, SHA512SUM0/SUM1/SIG0/SIG1), guarded `sizeof(xlen) == 64` in riscv_insts_zkn.sail, are present in the RV32 decoder anyway: the guard was lost in the generated C (base RV64 instructions such as addiw are correctly absent). Their execute clauses assert xlen == 64, so an RV32 encoding of one (TestRIG riscv_unstructured: aes64dsm 0x3fd80933) stopped the model with a Sail assertion. Each of the 22 blocks (both decoders) now starts with a jump to its own no-match label ("local: RV64-only scalar crypto, guard lost in the RV32 C"), so they decode as illegal. Latent since the C was vendored; not reported upstream.
