- 2026-10-12 generated C and c_emulator only (no .sail mirror, as above): Smepmp 1.0, which Ibex implements whenever PMP is configured (ibex/doc/03_reference/pmp.rst) and the model lacked (TestRIG riscv_unstructured: csrrw mseccfg executed on the core, trapped in the model). c_emulator/ibex_platform_csrs.c holds mseccfg/mseccfgh (0x747/0x757, only with PMP; MML and MMWP sticky, RLB frozen at 0 once any pmpcfg.L is set; mseccfgh reads 0 and ignores writes, as Ibex documents) and the rules, from the ratified Smepmp 1.0 text: the MML truth table (section 2.1) for a matching entry, MMWP default deny and MML no-execute for M-mode accesses matching no entry, RLB bypassing locks, and with MML the RW=01 Shared-Region encodings kept and new executable M-mode-only/locked Shared-Region rules refused unless RLB. Hooks ("Local patch (VENDORED_FROM 2026-10-12, Smepmp)"): top of pmpCheckPerms (MML table), pmpWriteCfg (replaced by ibex_smepmp_write_cfg, identical without MML/RLB), pmpWriteAddr (RLB), the M-mode default at the end of pmpCheck, and writeCSR (passes "any pmpcfg.L set" before an mseccfg write). The RVFI-DII fetch check (rvfi_fetch_pmp_denied) calls pmpCheck, so fetches follow the same rules. Checked with a C harness (17 cases: CSR stickiness and RLB freezing, MMWP load fault, MML fetch fault, a locked R/X rule under MML, rule 4b refusal, RW=01 with and without MML, RLB lock bypass).
