- 2026-10-19 riscv_insts_zicsr.sail writeCSR (0x320) + generated C (zwriteCSR, the Ibex-CSR branch): a write to mcountinhibit sets minstret_increment from the IR value written, so the writing instruction is counted as Ibex counts it (doc/03_reference/performance_counters.rst): an instruction that sets IR is not counted, one that clears IR is. The RISC-V specifications leave this edge open; the step decided it from the old value, the opposite on both edges, so every IR toggle put the model's minstret one off the core's (TestRIG riscv 2026-10-19: minstret reads 1 to 6 apart in both directions once they were compared). The core's behaviour was measured by the self-checking UVM test minstret_exact (checks 50-57: 1 and 6, the same after a load, after a divide and in every pass, seeds 1-3).
